# One job in flight (rhizome-agent)

Atticus rattles ideas by speech-to-text. He does not cue "do this now" vs "log that." Infer. Do not ask him to classify.

## The mechanism

Cursor todos are the queue. At most one item is `in_progress`.

| Todo status | Means |
|---|---|
| `in_progress` | Doing. Exactly one. |
| `pending` | Queued. Arrival order. Next up is the oldest pending product item. |
| `cancelled` | Parked. He said later, maybe, or stop that item. |
| `completed` | Done in the tree this session. Commit still waits for CPR. |

A new product bug, screenshot, or "we need X" becomes `pending`. It does not steal `in_progress`.

A how-does-it-work question gets a short answer. Then return to `in_progress`.

An opinion, a maybe, or "decide later" is `cancelled` (Parked). No code.

"Stop" stops Doing. "Now" moves that item to `in_progress` and the old Doing back to `pending`. Those words are optional.

Do not start a second product change until the current slice is finished or parked.

## Failure mode this rule exists to stop

Wrong: the newest line becomes the job. The old job sits half-done. A footer list claims we are tracking it.

Right: finish the slice, or park it, then start the oldest pending item.

The Doing / Queued / Wanted / Parked / Done footer is a read of the todos. It is not the work. Keep the list when Doing is empty.

## When any bucket has an item, end the turn with

- Doing (the `in_progress` title, or `none`)
- Queued (pending titles, oldest first)
- Wanted (keep this idea, not started)
- Parked
- Done

## After that list, offer to delegate

If two or more queued items are still open, ask whether to send some to subagents. Do not spawn until he picks. This chat keeps at most one `in_progress` job.

For each candidate, name four facts in one line: title, difficulty (S/M/L), urgency (now / soon / later), and whether it is independent of Doing (different files, no product call).

Good to offer: well-specified, independent of Doing, can finish without him. Writers use a git worktree. Do not write in the shared tree in parallel.

Do not offer: the current Doing, Parked items, CPR, or anything that still needs a product call from him.

Use the structured question UI when more than one item is a candidate. Silence after the offer means no. He can also say "now" on one item and leave the rest queued.

## Chimed-in work while subagents are already running

He will add notes while this chat is mid-slice. If the note is an agreed product change and its files do not overlap Doing, append it to a running subagent (`resume`) or start one. Do not wait for another pick round.

Keep this chat on Doing. Do not give two writers the same files. A steer on the current panel stays here.
